From 00aae34a5eb74a45297d4f44f33cb1330a716c2d Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Elia Palme <elia.palme@cscs.ch>
Date: Tue, 1 Sep 2026 22:20:29 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] [misc] fix: build nested tensors unconditionally in
 list_of_dict_to_tensordict

list_of_dict_to_tensordict decided dense-vs-ragged per field with
`all(item.shape == val_list[0].shape for item in val_list)`. That check is
vacuously true for a length-1 list (this function is called once per rollout
output, so the list is frequently length 1) and also true whenever several
genuinely ragged items coincidentally share a length -- most commonly a group
of GRPO rollout responses that all saturate max_response_length. In both cases
it silently torch.stack()'d ragged per-sample tensors (input_ids, responses,
position_ids, ...) into a dense [N, L] tensor, and downstream code that expects
a nested tensor then raised
`AttributeError: 'Tensor' object has no attribute 'offsets'`
-- observed from both current callers, the TransferQueue rollout-write path
(verl/trainer/ppo/v1/agent_loop_tq.py) and the padding upsampler
(verl/trainer/ppo/padding_utils.py).

Replace the shape-equality heuristic: non-tensor / empty -> NonTensorStack,
all-scalar (0-d) tensors -> torch.stack (no dimension to be ragged along),
everything else -> nested_tensor_from_tensor_list (already used unconditionally
elsewhere in this file for chunking/dispatch). The old `else` branch was
already torch.nested.as_nested_tensor, so the only behavior change is that
uniform-shape multi-element tensor fields now go nested instead of stacked.

Add tests/utils/test_tensordict_utils_on_cpu.py covering the length-1,
same-length, variable-length, scalar and non-tensor cases.

Signed-off-by: Elia Palme <elia.palme@cscs.ch>
---
 tests/utils/test_tensordict_utils_on_cpu.py | 68 +++++++++++++++++++++
 verl/utils/tensordict_utils.py              | 31 +++++-----
 2 files changed, 85 insertions(+), 14 deletions(-)
 create mode 100644 tests/utils/test_tensordict_utils_on_cpu.py

diff --git a/tests/utils/test_tensordict_utils_on_cpu.py b/tests/utils/test_tensordict_utils_on_cpu.py
new file mode 100644
index 00000000000..0607a0a9464
--- /dev/null
+++ b/tests/utils/test_tensordict_utils_on_cpu.py
@@ -0,0 +1,68 @@
